        "Content": "Please note: Some images used in this listing are projected or digitally dressed images. These have been included to help illustrate the potential layout, scale, and possible use of the rooms. They are for visual guidance only and should not be taken as an exact representation of the current furnishings or finishes.\r\n\r\n\r\n•  Superb opportunity to acquire a derelict old-world cottage on approx. 0.5 acre \r\n•  Highly desirable Jenkinstown, Co. Kilkenny location \r\n•  Approximately 10 minutes’ drive from the Kilkenny City Ring Road \r\n•  Wonderful combination of location, setting and development potential \r\n•  Attractive and peaceful countryside setting \r\n•  Excellent opportunity to restore, extend or reimagine the existing cottage,\r\n    subject to planning permission \r\n•  Property has been idle for many years, offering potential to qualify for\r\n    vacant/derelict property grant assistance, subject to eligibility and approval \r\n•  Can be sold subject to planning permission, offering additional reassurance \r\n    to prospective purchasers \r\n•  Convenient to a local National School, Close to Jenkinstown Wood and Park,\r\n    renowned for its mature woodland and scenic walks \r\n•  Easy access to Kilkenny City and its extensive amenities \r\n•  Ideal opportunity for those looking to create a bespoke countryside home \r\n•  Rare chance to acquire a property with character, potential and an \r\n    exceptional location\r\n\r\n\r\nCoischoille represents a phenomenal opportunity to acquire a derelict old-world cottage standing on approximately 0.5 acres, in what is undoubtedly one of County Kilkenny’s most attractive and desirable rural locations.\r\nFor anyone seeking a renovation project, a countryside retreat or the opportunity to create a new home in a wonderful setting, Coischoille is a property with enormous potential. The combination of location, setting and surroundings makes this a particularly exciting offering.\r\nThe property enjoys the tranquillity and character of a rural setting while remaining remarkably convenient to Kilkenny City. The Kilkenny City Ring Road is approximately a ten-minute drive away, providing easy access to the city and its extensive range of schools, shops, services, employment and recreational amenities.\r\nJenkinstown itself is renowned for its beautiful countryside and mature woodland setting. The property is conveniently located close to a local National School, while Jenkinstown Wood and Park are also nearby, offering wonderful opportunities to enjoy walking and the natural beauty for which the area is so well known.\r\nThe existing cottage has been idle for many years and is now in derelict condition. While substantial works will be required, its condition and history of vacancy may offer significant potential to qualify for available vacant and derelict property refurbishment grant assistance, subject to the relevant criteria and approvals.\r\nStanding on approximately half an acre, the site offers the prospective purchaser an opportunity to explore the restoration and extension of the existing cottage or potentially an alternative residential proposal, all subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\nImportantly, the property can be sold subject to the purchaser obtaining planning permission, making this an especially attractive proposition for those wishing to secure a superb site and location while progressing their plans for a future home.\r\nFor those with the vision to recognise its potential, Coischoille offers the opportunity to create something truly special in a magnificent County Kilkenny setting. \r\n\r\nThese particulars are issued strictly on the understanding that they do not form part of any contract and are provided, without liability, as a general guide only to what is being offered subject to contract and availability. They are not to be constructed as containing any representation of fact upon which any interested party is entitled to rely. Any intending purchaser or lessee should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the accuracy of these particulars. The vendor or lessor do not make, give or imply nor is Fran Grincell or its staff authorized to make, give or imply any representation or warranty whatsoever in respect of this property. No responsibility can be accepted for any expenses incurred by intending purchasers in inspecting properties which have been sold, let or withdrawn. \r\n\r\n#THINKING OF SELLING EMAIL OR CALL FOR SALES ADVICE PACK#"
